# The index and the archive it came from never enter the build context.
#
# Neither is COPYed by the Dockerfile, so this is not what keeps them out of
# the image — it keeps them out of the daemon's reach entirely. A build context
# is uploaded whole before any COPY runs, and the archive is a gigabyte of the
# client's data with real email addresses in it. Excluding it here means a
# careless COPY added later cannot pick it up either.
*.zip
index.sqlite
index/
build-report.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
reports/
.git/
